  "id": "Compound::DB00207 - Gene::1548",
  "verbalization": "Azithromycin is implicated in the development of Drug-induced Hepatitis and Drug-induced Liver Injury, both of which are associated with Dapagliflozin. Dapagliflozin, a sodium-glucose cotransporter inhibitor, binds to Cyp2a6, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Azithromycin may influence Cyp2a6 activity. The shared pathway through Dapagliflozin and Cyp2a6 indicates a possible interaction between Azithromycin and Cyp2a6, likely through the modulation of Cyp2a6 expression or function. The evidence suggests that Azithromycin may indirectly affect Cyp2a6 by promoting the binding of Dapagliflozin, which in turn alters Cyp2a6 activity. This relationship is supported by the presence of a common ancestor in the glycosyl compound class, reinforcing the biochemical link between Azithromycin and Cyp2a6.",
